<description>
The function `SafeInt32Add` safely adds two 32-bit signed integers, `arg1` and `arg2`, and stores the result in the location pointed to by `result`. It returns `true` if the addition is successful, and `false` if the addition would result in an integer overflow. The function handles overflow by catching a `dng_exception` thrown by the underlying addition logic.
</description>

<requirements>

<requirement>
The 'result' pointer must not be NULL. This is to prevent a null pointer dereference when the function attempts to write the addition result.
</requirement>
<requirement>
